 --help mechanism ('the command detects -h/--help in argv and prints parser.format_help()', so help is GENERATED from argparse flag definitions) does not achieve its goal: for claim/transition, --help/-h is intercepted at the top-level dispatcher BEFORE the command handler runs and is served from byte-exact golden package data, so the command's own format_help() branch is unreachable dead code on the real invocation path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f586aa7fc67161277","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Behavioral fidelity ('--help/-h reconciled with add_help=False'); AC1","norm_id":"nd705b34acb78bf28","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`rebar claim --help` — dispatcher serves help/claim.txt; the planned format_help() branch is never reached","`rebar transition --help` — same, served from help/transition.txt"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that --help remains served by the top-level dispatcher from golden help/claim.txt & help/transition.txt (byte-exact, pinned by tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py::test_sub_help_equals_help_sub and test_schema_coverage.py), and that this refactor is PARSE-ONLY — the argparse parser is not the help source. Remove the AC1 clause asserting help is generated from the flag definitions, or, if generated help is genuinely wanted, add explicit scope to reroute the dispatcher intercept and regenerate/repoint the goldens (and reconcile the equivalence + schema-coverage tests).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes